WEBVTT

00:00:16.391 --> 00:00:19.311
[vacuum whirring distantly]

00:00:36.537 --> 00:00:40.999
"You're... a... b-b...

00:00:43.043 --> 00:00:44.544
big...

00:00:44.628 --> 00:00:47.798
g... girl... now."

00:00:47.923 --> 00:00:49.549
[woman] Marcy?

00:00:49.675 --> 00:00:52.427
I gotta leave early tonight.
You all right alone?

00:00:53.303 --> 00:00:54.930
I'm... I'm fine.

00:00:55.055 --> 00:00:58.183
Don't forget to take your break.
You work too hard.

00:00:58.308 --> 00:01:00.852
I won't. I won't.

00:01:00.936 --> 00:01:03.063
Bye, Tory.

00:01:22.874 --> 00:01:24.001
[muffled screaming]

00:01:24.084 --> 00:01:25.627
[screaming intensifies]

00:01:30.882 --> 00:01:31.925
-[slapping glass]
-Don't!

00:01:32.009 --> 00:01:34.386
[crying out in terror]

00:01:34.469 --> 00:01:35.554
Stop!

00:01:35.637 --> 00:01:39.391
-[Marcy pounding on glass]
-[Tory wails]

00:01:49.151 --> 00:01:50.527
[shattering]

00:02:02.164 --> 00:02:03.165
[snickers]

00:02:06.793 --> 00:02:09.755
[faint ringing in Marcy's head]

00:02:14.635 --> 00:02:17.220
[echoing of clock ticking]

00:02:43.372 --> 00:02:44.414
[Marcy groaning]

00:02:44.539 --> 00:02:45.999
[sinister laughter]

00:02:47.417 --> 00:02:48.919
[Marcy panting]

00:02:49.002 --> 00:02:52.047
David gave that to me!
David gave that to me!

00:02:53.548 --> 00:02:54.925
-David--
-[grunts]

00:03:01.264 --> 00:03:03.975
-[Marcy gasps]
-[ringing escalates]

00:03:04.059 --> 00:03:06.186
[cries out in pain] Ah!

00:03:07.312 --> 00:03:09.815
Ah!

00:03:10.899 --> 00:03:12.442
Ah!

00:03:16.822 --> 00:03:18.198
Aah!

00:03:20.158 --> 00:03:22.202
[Marcy screams in agony]

00:03:25.831 --> 00:03:28.208
-[gasps]
-[ringing stops]

00:03:37.968 --> 00:03:39.219
That's mine.

00:03:40.470 --> 00:03:42.347
Holy shit.

00:03:42.472 --> 00:03:44.307
[groaning]

00:04:10.250 --> 00:04:13.336
[faint cheering of spectators]

00:04:18.008 --> 00:04:20.177
[crowd cheering]

00:04:22.429 --> 00:04:24.139
[crowd shouting]

00:04:45.076 --> 00:04:46.119
[man] Trevor.

00:04:46.203 --> 00:04:48.288
You stay down, man.
He's better than you.

00:04:50.332 --> 00:04:52.334
-You can stay down, man!
-Shut up!

00:04:54.294 --> 00:04:56.046
You should've stayed down.

00:05:10.352 --> 00:05:11.394
[heavy thud]

00:05:11.478 --> 00:05:14.314
Trevor! Trevor!

00:05:17.442 --> 00:05:19.236
[faint ringing in Trevor's head]

00:05:19.319 --> 00:05:20.529
[ringing intensifies]

00:05:20.612 --> 00:05:22.113
[screams]

00:05:23.448 --> 00:05:24.574
Aah!

00:05:31.498 --> 00:05:32.707
[ringing stops]

00:05:49.975 --> 00:05:52.018
I concede the fight.

00:05:54.854 --> 00:05:58.149
[thrash metal
plays on record player]

00:06:01.361 --> 00:06:03.363
-Do we need to cut it?
-Nah.

00:06:27.387 --> 00:06:29.389
[faint ringing rises]

00:06:34.019 --> 00:06:35.562
[crying out]

00:06:37.314 --> 00:06:39.399
Ahh!

00:06:41.443 --> 00:06:43.445
-[gasps]
-[ringing stops]

00:06:52.579 --> 00:06:54.664
[panting]

00:07:02.964 --> 00:07:06.092
[pants]

00:07:15.852 --> 00:07:18.104
[baby crying]

00:07:26.071 --> 00:07:27.030
It's okay.

00:07:27.113 --> 00:07:28.448
It's okay.
It's almost ready.

00:07:29.491 --> 00:07:32.077
-[vehicle approaches]
-[engine shuts off]

00:07:33.578 --> 00:07:36.039
[baby crying louder]

00:07:39.459 --> 00:07:41.378
[man] Carly?

00:07:41.461 --> 00:07:43.129
Carly?

00:07:43.254 --> 00:07:45.131
[Carly] You're not
coming in like that.

00:07:45.256 --> 00:07:47.133
You promised, Jeff.

00:07:47.258 --> 00:07:49.135
[Jeff] Come on, Carly.
Don't make me mad.

00:07:49.260 --> 00:07:51.096
I gotta take a piss.

00:07:55.100 --> 00:07:57.519
[lock turning]

00:08:00.355 --> 00:08:02.983
[baby cries]

00:08:07.404 --> 00:08:09.197
Not supposed to be here
when you drink.

00:08:09.280 --> 00:08:11.282
-[Jeff] Why is he crying?
-He's just hungry.

00:08:11.408 --> 00:08:12.534
Give him something to eat!

00:08:12.617 --> 00:08:14.661
I'm warming it up.

00:08:16.538 --> 00:08:17.789
What is this shit?

00:08:18.915 --> 00:08:21.668
It's baby food.
He's a baby, Jeff.

00:08:25.922 --> 00:08:27.298
-[crack]
-[gasps]

00:08:27.424 --> 00:08:29.551
[Jeff] Don't talk to me
like I'm an idiot.

00:08:29.634 --> 00:08:30.677
[baby cries]

00:08:30.802 --> 00:08:32.762
[Carly gasps]

00:08:39.144 --> 00:08:41.021
[ringing in Carly's head]

00:08:42.147 --> 00:08:44.524
[ringing intensifies]

00:08:44.607 --> 00:08:47.527
[Carly gasps]

00:08:47.652 --> 00:08:48.778
[screaming]

00:08:48.862 --> 00:08:50.947
[Jeff] This is bullshit.
Yo, come on!

00:08:51.031 --> 00:08:53.158
Hey, all you're doing
is pissing me off!

00:08:53.241 --> 00:08:56.161
[ringing continues]

00:08:58.872 --> 00:09:00.373
[ringing stops]

00:09:02.500 --> 00:09:04.544
[panting]

00:09:12.677 --> 00:09:15.180
[Jeff] Listen, I'm sorry.

00:09:15.263 --> 00:09:16.431
You make me crazy.

00:09:16.514 --> 00:09:18.641
You need to go.

00:09:22.437 --> 00:09:23.688
[Jeff] All right.

00:09:23.813 --> 00:09:26.191
I'm going.

00:09:30.945 --> 00:09:32.655
[door shuts]

00:09:37.494 --> 00:09:39.621
[♪♪♪]

00:10:02.602 --> 00:10:04.604
[text alert chimes]

00:10:09.192 --> 00:10:10.360
"Ruok"?

00:10:13.571 --> 00:10:14.614
"Ru-ok"?

00:10:16.950 --> 00:10:18.243
"Ruok..."

00:10:18.326 --> 00:10:19.536
[mom] You're up early.

00:10:19.619 --> 00:10:21.621
[footsteps]

00:10:25.250 --> 00:10:27.001
-[kissing]
-The headache wake you?

00:10:27.127 --> 00:10:28.586
The sound of birds.

00:10:30.755 --> 00:10:33.883
[dad] Know how stupid it is
to pick a fight before a game?

00:10:34.008 --> 00:10:36.386
How do you throw a football
with a broken hand?

00:10:36.469 --> 00:10:39.764
[mom] Doctors are more
concerned with his concussion.

00:10:39.848 --> 00:10:41.766
[dad] You blow your chance
at a scholarship,

00:10:41.850 --> 00:10:43.518
you better start
learning to flip burgers.

00:10:43.601 --> 00:10:46.771
All right.
You scoot upstairs. Get ready.

00:10:46.896 --> 00:10:49.566
They wanted to see you again
in the morning.

00:10:49.649 --> 00:10:50.525
Thank you, Mom.

00:10:57.240 --> 00:10:59.159
"Thank you, Mom"?

00:10:59.242 --> 00:11:00.785
Who the hell's that?

00:11:01.995 --> 00:11:04.664
-[baby cooing]
-[keys clacking]

00:11:21.764 --> 00:11:23.808
[keys clacking]

00:11:39.324 --> 00:11:41.576
[door opens]

00:11:47.081 --> 00:11:48.207
[man] Philip Pearson?

00:11:49.417 --> 00:11:51.711
Tried to find you
at the university.

00:11:51.836 --> 00:11:52.837
I'm Detective Gower.

00:11:52.921 --> 00:11:54.589
"Gower"?

00:11:54.714 --> 00:11:56.424
[Gower] Your roommate
passed away last night.

00:11:59.469 --> 00:12:02.472
You don't seem surprised.

00:12:09.854 --> 00:12:11.981
[knocking on door]

00:12:13.358 --> 00:12:14.484
[man] It's me.

00:12:23.117 --> 00:12:24.744
[Marcy] David?
[David] Yeah.

00:12:27.372 --> 00:12:30.625
Oh! That's...
not appropriate.

00:12:30.750 --> 00:12:32.210
Marcy, put some clothes on.

00:12:34.879 --> 00:12:36.130
Yeah, I can't, uh...

00:12:36.214 --> 00:12:39.759
be your boyfriend, Marcy,
w-we talked about this.

00:12:43.972 --> 00:12:45.139
What's that?

00:12:46.891 --> 00:12:48.309
[Marcy] Oh...

00:12:48.393 --> 00:12:50.269
What happened?

00:12:50.395 --> 00:12:52.397
[Marcy] Uh... I fell.

00:12:52.522 --> 00:12:55.149
[David] And you just went home?

00:12:55.274 --> 00:12:57.193
Oh, kiddo, are you okay?
Does it hurt?

00:12:57.276 --> 00:12:59.404
I'm fine.

00:12:59.487 --> 00:13:01.406
[David] Well, I know
going to the doctor's

00:13:01.489 --> 00:13:03.866
not your favorite thing
in the world, but...

00:13:06.160 --> 00:13:09.288
That's a--
That's a nasty cut.

00:13:11.416 --> 00:13:12.667
Is this appropriate?

00:13:12.792 --> 00:13:16.170
Appropriate? Sure.

00:13:16.295 --> 00:13:18.548
[stammers]
Maybe some underwear.

00:13:22.301 --> 00:13:23.720
[Gower] So you skipped out?

00:13:23.803 --> 00:13:25.805
[Philip] I just walked.

00:13:25.930 --> 00:13:27.181
Uh-huh.

00:13:27.265 --> 00:13:29.934
And the loaded syringe
we found on the table,

00:13:30.059 --> 00:13:32.270
that wasn't meant for you?

00:13:33.688 --> 00:13:35.732
Uh, what difference
does it make?

00:13:35.815 --> 00:13:40.319
Did Stephen inject himself,
or did you do it for him?

00:13:40.445 --> 00:13:43.239
Because your prints
were found on both syringes.

00:13:43.322 --> 00:13:45.950
I was there, but then I-I left.

00:13:46.075 --> 00:13:47.827
Yeah...

00:13:47.910 --> 00:13:50.329
because you knew
he was gonna O.D.

00:13:53.833 --> 00:13:55.126
Yeah, you knew.

00:13:55.209 --> 00:14:00.214
You know, a phone call to 911
could've saved his life.

00:14:00.298 --> 00:14:02.800
That's cold, Philip.

00:14:04.594 --> 00:14:06.596
Either way,
you have got a problem.

00:14:08.473 --> 00:14:10.391
On top of your drug problem.

00:14:10.475 --> 00:14:12.393
[Philip]
I don't have a drug problem.

00:14:12.477 --> 00:14:14.145
[Gower]
I know who your dealer is.

00:14:14.228 --> 00:14:15.730
I know how much you buy.

00:14:15.855 --> 00:14:18.357
I know who your friends are
and where you're from.

00:14:18.441 --> 00:14:20.985
You have no idea where I'm from.

00:14:21.110 --> 00:14:22.904
You inject somebody,
they O.D.,

00:14:22.987 --> 00:14:24.530
that's manslaughter.

00:14:24.614 --> 00:14:25.615
I have the right

00:14:25.740 --> 00:14:27.283
to court-appointed
legal counsel, yes?

00:14:27.367 --> 00:14:30.328
Sure you don't want
to call your parents instead?

00:14:34.749 --> 00:14:38.336
You think you're sick now,
wait till your lawyer shows up.

00:14:39.879 --> 00:14:41.589
[David]
I'm proud of you, you know.

00:14:43.716 --> 00:14:46.427
What? What for?

00:14:46.511 --> 00:14:48.388
You got knocked
in the head last night,

00:14:48.513 --> 00:14:49.764
and you're...

00:14:49.889 --> 00:14:52.266
you know, the naked thing,
that-- that was weird,

00:14:52.392 --> 00:14:55.603
but otherwise, you're handling
this amazingly well.

00:15:00.900 --> 00:15:02.527
Hey, it's Thursday.

00:15:03.903 --> 00:15:05.196
It's reading-aloud day.

00:15:05.279 --> 00:15:08.616
There's no point in wasting
time sitting on a bus.

00:15:09.742 --> 00:15:12.578
It's just me.
It can be anything at all.

00:15:12.662 --> 00:15:14.664
Think I got your favorite.

00:15:14.789 --> 00:15:16.457
"Police were forced
to use tear gas

00:15:16.541 --> 00:15:17.667
to disperse a crowd

00:15:17.750 --> 00:15:19.293
shortly after
a not-guilty verdict

00:15:19.377 --> 00:15:21.796
was announced out--"

00:15:27.427 --> 00:15:28.803
What?

00:15:28.886 --> 00:15:31.055
What-- What's wrong?

00:15:33.266 --> 00:15:35.435
[birds singing]

00:15:45.778 --> 00:15:48.030
You didn't answer your cell.

00:15:49.782 --> 00:15:51.701
What did they say?

00:15:51.784 --> 00:15:53.828
I have a concussion.

00:15:53.953 --> 00:15:55.079
Oh, no.

00:15:55.163 --> 00:15:57.957
Will you be able to play
in the game next week?

00:15:58.040 --> 00:15:59.709
The doctor said that...

00:15:59.792 --> 00:16:01.586
if I hadn't walked away
from the fight,

00:16:01.711 --> 00:16:02.712
I might have died.

00:16:03.963 --> 00:16:05.756
Does it hurt now?

00:16:05.840 --> 00:16:07.216
A little.

00:16:09.594 --> 00:16:10.845
Are your folks home?

00:16:10.970 --> 00:16:13.556
No. Why?

00:16:16.058 --> 00:16:18.478
Oh, I don't think
that we should, Rene,

00:16:18.561 --> 00:16:19.729
'cause my concussion.

00:16:19.812 --> 00:16:21.606
Let me make you feel better.

00:16:24.233 --> 00:16:26.903
Look. Please, stop.

00:16:26.986 --> 00:16:29.989
-I don't think that we should.
-Are you breaking up with me?

00:16:30.114 --> 00:16:31.324
No!

00:16:32.742 --> 00:16:36.871
If anything...
I want to be closer to you.

00:16:36.996 --> 00:16:38.623
There are things
I don't remember.

00:16:38.748 --> 00:16:39.665
Things about me?

00:16:39.749 --> 00:16:41.876
It's more things about myself.

00:16:41.959 --> 00:16:44.253
The doctor said
that a concussion as bad as this

00:16:44.378 --> 00:16:47.381
can cause changes in personality
and memory loss,

00:16:47.507 --> 00:16:48.883
that the only treatment
is time--

00:16:48.966 --> 00:16:52.678
that in time I'll be the person
I was before the concussion.

00:16:52.762 --> 00:16:55.515
I need you to help me
remember who that person is.

00:16:56.516 --> 00:17:00.394
Y-You want me to help you
find yourself?

00:17:00.520 --> 00:17:02.438
Trev...

00:17:02.522 --> 00:17:03.856
That is so beautiful.

00:17:07.443 --> 00:17:08.945
[Trevor] Look...

00:17:09.028 --> 00:17:10.947
You should go.

00:17:11.072 --> 00:17:13.449
[Rene] I don't want to,
but I will.

00:17:13.533 --> 00:17:15.660
That's how much I love you.

00:17:38.474 --> 00:17:40.935
Daddy's coming.

00:17:51.320 --> 00:17:52.238
You busy right now?

00:17:53.239 --> 00:17:54.115
Not yet.

00:17:54.198 --> 00:17:55.866
We just got sent a red flag.

00:17:57.368 --> 00:17:59.495
Can't you handle it?
I'm all over Jonas Walker.

00:17:59.579 --> 00:18:01.163
[Forbes] I'm in court
today and tomorrow.

00:18:01.247 --> 00:18:02.665
[MacLaren]
What's the flag?

00:18:02.748 --> 00:18:04.250
Potential cell.

00:18:04.375 --> 00:18:08.379
Encrypted communication
in the deep web.

00:18:08.504 --> 00:18:10.506
I have no idea
what I'm looking at.

00:18:10.590 --> 00:18:13.551
Analyst who flagged it is hoping
that they're just gamers.

00:18:13.634 --> 00:18:15.011
Who travel, apparently.

00:18:15.094 --> 00:18:17.138
[Forbes] Those GPS coordinates
correspond

00:18:17.221 --> 00:18:18.639
to an abandoned building
downtown.

00:18:18.723 --> 00:18:19.807
[MacLaren]
And what's a "T.E.L.L."?

00:18:19.890 --> 00:18:21.267
[Forbes]
I asked the same question.

00:18:21.392 --> 00:18:23.102
They ran it
and nothing showed up.

00:18:24.854 --> 00:18:26.272
Aw, shit, I'm late.

00:18:26.355 --> 00:18:29.025
It's probably nothing, but...

00:18:29.150 --> 00:18:31.319
Yeah, yeah. I got it.
I'll let you know.

00:18:31.402 --> 00:18:32.445
Have fun in court.

00:18:32.528 --> 00:18:33.321
[Forbes chuckles]

00:18:33.404 --> 00:18:34.572
[Forbes] Make sure Jonas Walker

00:18:34.655 --> 00:18:37.658
doesn't shoot anyone
while I'm gone.

00:18:37.742 --> 00:18:40.161
You didn't coach her?

00:18:40.244 --> 00:18:43.122
No amount of coaching
can do that.

00:18:44.415 --> 00:18:46.667
[door shuts]

00:18:46.751 --> 00:18:47.793
[doctor] You recognize

00:18:47.918 --> 00:18:51.047
Marcy has a significant
intellectual disability.

00:18:51.130 --> 00:18:52.548
Yeah. "Had."

00:18:52.673 --> 00:18:54.675
You want to think
something wonderful's happened,

00:18:54.800 --> 00:18:56.344
but no traumatic brain injury

00:18:56.427 --> 00:18:58.679
is going to increase
intellectual capacity.

00:18:58.804 --> 00:18:59.805
It's just not possible.

00:18:59.889 --> 00:19:01.432
Which brings us back
to "miracle."

00:19:01.557 --> 00:19:03.726
[doctor] Assuming that there was
a traumatic injury,

00:19:03.809 --> 00:19:05.561
likely a concussion,

00:19:05.686 --> 00:19:07.480
the most common symptoms
would be memory loss,

00:19:07.563 --> 00:19:08.606
change in personality--

00:19:08.689 --> 00:19:09.690
So...

00:19:09.774 --> 00:19:11.442
What if this is the real Marcy?

00:19:12.401 --> 00:19:13.277
Seriously?

00:19:13.361 --> 00:19:16.489
Up until the age of 18,
Marcy lived in an institution,

00:19:16.572 --> 00:19:19.075
one with a reputation
for neglect and abuse,

00:19:19.158 --> 00:19:21.702
right up until the time
it was shut down.

00:19:21.786 --> 00:19:23.079
She doesn't talk about that.

00:19:23.162 --> 00:19:24.830
[doctor]
Maybe the "Marcy" we knew

00:19:24.955 --> 00:19:26.707
was her way of coping there,

00:19:26.791 --> 00:19:29.085
her way of making people
look after her,

00:19:29.168 --> 00:19:31.712
and she just continued that
behavior after her release,

00:19:31.796 --> 00:19:33.130
and when she hit her head...

00:19:33.214 --> 00:19:35.341
She just forgot
who she was pretending to be?

00:19:35.424 --> 00:19:36.342
That's crazy.

00:19:36.467 --> 00:19:37.843
[doctor] It's infinitely
more possible

00:19:37.968 --> 00:19:39.845
than her I.Q.
doubling overnight.

00:19:39.970 --> 00:19:41.847
I've been her caseworker
since her release.

00:19:41.972 --> 00:19:45.351
-That was over a year ago!
-My case in point.

00:19:45.476 --> 00:19:47.353
You got her
a subsidized apartment,

00:19:47.478 --> 00:19:49.105
a job at the library.

00:19:49.188 --> 00:19:51.524
You see her
four or five times a week--

00:19:51.607 --> 00:19:52.983
You're saying she played me?

00:19:53.067 --> 00:19:55.361
The most innocent soul
I've ever met.

00:19:55.444 --> 00:19:57.780
Played the system.
Fooled me, too.

00:19:57.863 --> 00:20:00.616
So she could live in a flophouse
full of crackheads,

00:20:00.700 --> 00:20:03.494
work nights at a library
for the rest of her adult life?

00:20:03.619 --> 00:20:05.121
No, you're right.
She's a mastermind.

00:20:05.204 --> 00:20:07.123
She's a James Bond villain.

00:20:07.248 --> 00:20:09.500
[doctor] Neural pathways
can't spring up overnight.

00:20:09.625 --> 00:20:11.001
Vocabulary doesn't
come out of nowhere.

00:20:11.085 --> 00:20:12.837
And what's happened
to her stutter?

00:20:15.256 --> 00:20:17.216
Is something wrong?

00:20:18.843 --> 00:20:22.263
[straining to read]
<i>"You're... a...</i>

00:20:22.388 --> 00:20:26.016
<i>big...</i>

00:20:26.100 --> 00:20:28.185
<i>girl...</i>

00:20:28.269 --> 00:20:29.895
<i>now,"</i>

00:20:30.020 --> 00:20:33.858
<i>said... Mary...</i>

00:20:35.526 --> 00:20:36.652
[mouthing sounds]

00:20:36.736 --> 00:20:38.779
<i>T...</i>

00:20:38.863 --> 00:20:40.948
<i>Tee-- Teacher.</i>

00:20:41.031 --> 00:20:42.908
-[panting]
-[woman] <i>Good.</i>

00:20:43.033 --> 00:20:45.161
[doctor] Do you remember that?

00:20:46.537 --> 00:20:49.248
It was just a few months ago.

00:20:50.791 --> 00:20:52.918
I don't understand.

00:20:53.002 --> 00:20:54.170
[doctor] Neither do we.

00:20:54.253 --> 00:20:58.549
I'd like to find out
what else you don't remember.

00:20:58.674 --> 00:21:00.593
It's okay... I'm here.

00:21:00.676 --> 00:21:02.678
[doctor]
Let's start with yesterday.

00:21:02.762 --> 00:21:04.680
Where were you?

00:21:04.764 --> 00:21:05.931
At the library.

00:21:06.807 --> 00:21:07.683
Good.

00:21:07.808 --> 00:21:09.685
[doctor] What did you do
at the library?

00:21:09.810 --> 00:21:13.481
I'm a librarian, so I was...

00:21:13.564 --> 00:21:15.483
So you were
checking books in and out,

00:21:15.566 --> 00:21:17.985
helping folks find
what they were looking for?

00:21:18.068 --> 00:21:19.195
Yes.

00:21:19.278 --> 00:21:21.989
[doctor] And can you name
one of those people?

00:21:22.072 --> 00:21:22.948
David.

00:21:23.032 --> 00:21:24.742
Uh, to do research.

00:21:24.825 --> 00:21:26.076
He's a reporter.

00:21:26.202 --> 00:21:27.703
Marcy, stop.

00:21:29.455 --> 00:21:31.540
What's wrong?

00:21:33.584 --> 00:21:36.086
You being a librarian,

00:21:36.212 --> 00:21:39.465
me going there to do research
for a newspaper I work for--

00:21:39.548 --> 00:21:41.592
those are all part
of a profile page

00:21:41.675 --> 00:21:43.219
that we made up.

00:21:43.344 --> 00:21:44.970
That's my profile.

00:21:45.054 --> 00:21:47.139
We created it as an exercise...

00:21:47.223 --> 00:21:50.226
so I could teach you
about social media

00:21:50.351 --> 00:21:52.353
and other things
about the world.

00:21:53.479 --> 00:21:55.481
Remember?

00:21:56.732 --> 00:21:58.234
You're not a librarian.

00:21:58.317 --> 00:21:59.902
You work there
as a cleaning lady.

00:21:59.985 --> 00:22:02.071
I'm not a reporter.

00:22:03.572 --> 00:22:06.242
I'm your social worker.

00:22:08.577 --> 00:22:11.914
So... so what...
you're saying is... that--

00:22:11.997 --> 00:22:14.124
We're just trying to understand.

00:22:14.250 --> 00:22:15.876
[gasps]

00:22:15.960 --> 00:22:17.253
[doctor] Marcy?

00:22:17.336 --> 00:22:18.504
[David] Marce?

00:22:18.587 --> 00:22:20.005
[Marcy gasping and gagging]

00:22:20.130 --> 00:22:22.091
[doctor] Marcy?
[David] Marcy!

00:22:28.514 --> 00:22:30.266
Take it you're not "Leticia."

00:22:30.391 --> 00:22:31.892
Wrong file.

00:22:33.978 --> 00:22:35.396
Go ahead, have a seat.

00:22:39.024 --> 00:22:39.984
Sit.

00:22:42.152 --> 00:22:45.656
You look like shit, Philip.
When was the last time you hit?

00:22:45.781 --> 00:22:47.408
-I don't use drugs.
-Come on, man.

00:22:47.491 --> 00:22:50.327
You don't have to pretend.
I know all about addiction.

00:22:50.411 --> 00:22:53.789
Trust me.
Mine's just legal.

00:22:53.914 --> 00:22:56.166
Have they talked
to you at all about

00:22:56.292 --> 00:22:58.043
the methadone program
they got going on?

00:22:58.168 --> 00:23:00.045
-What is it?
-Methadone?

00:23:00.170 --> 00:23:01.297
[Philip] Your addiction.

00:23:04.008 --> 00:23:05.050
Is it gambling?

00:23:07.303 --> 00:23:09.221
Cigarettes.

00:23:09.305 --> 00:23:11.223
Look, I'm just trying
to be <i>simpatico</i> here.

00:23:11.307 --> 00:23:13.058
Don't be a dick.

00:23:13.142 --> 00:23:14.393
I apologize.

00:23:15.811 --> 00:23:18.188
We're gonna plea.
You'll end up doing some time.

00:23:18.272 --> 00:23:19.356
There's no way around that.

00:23:19.440 --> 00:23:21.692
They got you two ways,
all right?

00:23:21.817 --> 00:23:22.818
But, in the meantime--

00:23:22.943 --> 00:23:25.446
Are you bound by
attorney-client privilege?

00:23:25.571 --> 00:23:27.948
Can you guarantee
your confidence

00:23:28.073 --> 00:23:30.993
if I tell you information
that can help us both?

00:23:31.076 --> 00:23:33.162
Absolutely. What?

00:23:48.093 --> 00:23:49.803
I'm so sorry.

00:23:54.099 --> 00:23:56.727
Come on, you love...

00:23:56.810 --> 00:23:58.854
You love making up
after we fight.

00:23:58.937 --> 00:24:01.148
That wasn't a fight.
You struck me.

00:24:01.231 --> 00:24:04.526
If I hadn't demanded you leave,
you would've struck me again.

00:24:04.610 --> 00:24:07.738
From now on, you'll be allowed
to see your son once a day

00:24:07.863 --> 00:24:09.740
for one hour,
time to be arranged.

00:24:09.865 --> 00:24:11.742
I see him when I wanna see him.

00:24:11.867 --> 00:24:15.996
Also, you'll provide
proper financial support.

00:24:16.080 --> 00:24:17.498
Okay. Okay, okay.

00:24:17.623 --> 00:24:19.625
I get it.

00:24:19.750 --> 00:24:22.378
Let me make it up to you.

00:24:22.503 --> 00:24:24.254
What do you want me to do?

00:24:27.508 --> 00:24:29.259
Change Jeffrey's diaper.

00:24:37.726 --> 00:24:38.936
[whistles]

00:24:39.019 --> 00:24:40.521
Hey! Phil!

00:24:41.772 --> 00:24:42.815
Hey.

00:24:42.898 --> 00:24:46.193
You got out quick.
What'd they tell you?

00:24:46.276 --> 00:24:48.404
They didn't say anything.
They just let me go.

00:24:48.487 --> 00:24:50.656
Come here, come here.
Come here for a sec.

00:24:55.661 --> 00:24:58.038
How did you know?

00:24:58.122 --> 00:25:00.082
Come on, man.
Three horses?

00:25:00.165 --> 00:25:01.792
Three races,
three different cities--

00:25:01.875 --> 00:25:03.669
all 20 to one or better?

00:25:03.752 --> 00:25:06.672
The bets were so stupid,
I had to go to three bookies.

00:25:06.755 --> 00:25:09.675
I wouldn't have done it if you
hadn't fronted the cash advance.

00:25:09.800 --> 00:25:11.969
It's all here, by the way,
with interest.

00:25:12.052 --> 00:25:14.430
Credit card's in there.

00:25:14.555 --> 00:25:15.973
Go ahead. Take it.

00:25:16.056 --> 00:25:17.057
Come on, come on.

00:25:20.561 --> 00:25:23.021
You gotta tell me.

00:25:24.189 --> 00:25:25.816
Do I still have
attorney-client privilege?

00:25:25.899 --> 00:25:27.693
Yeah, sure, whatever.
Yep. Yep.

00:25:28.902 --> 00:25:30.320
I'm from the future.

00:25:32.197 --> 00:25:34.199
Okay, I get it,
you can't tell me.

00:25:34.324 --> 00:25:37.703
But Phil...
you're gonna need me.

00:25:37.786 --> 00:25:39.580
The cops are gonna
be all over you.

00:25:39.705 --> 00:25:41.498
We gotta look after
each other here.

00:25:41.582 --> 00:25:42.833
All right?

00:25:42.958 --> 00:25:44.209
Oh, speaking of which--

00:25:44.293 --> 00:25:46.837
There's something extra in there
for you, from the lock-up.

00:25:48.380 --> 00:25:50.924
Just a little taste
so you don't get sick.

00:26:09.109 --> 00:26:11.445
[ticking]

00:26:13.489 --> 00:26:14.823
David?

00:26:16.575 --> 00:26:17.826
There she is.

00:26:21.705 --> 00:26:23.499
What happened?

00:26:23.624 --> 00:26:27.252
[David]
Dr. Lee says you had a seizure.

00:26:27.336 --> 00:26:30.631
It's the diminished capacity.
There's too much pre-existing damage.

00:26:30.714 --> 00:26:32.049
What?

00:26:32.132 --> 00:26:33.634
How did I get--?

00:26:33.759 --> 00:26:36.011
We had to take you
to the hospital.

00:26:36.094 --> 00:26:37.805
You've been out of it all day.

00:26:37.888 --> 00:26:40.516
Soon as you feel up to it,
they wanna run tests--

00:26:40.599 --> 00:26:42.392
-No, please.
-It's not up to me.

00:26:42.518 --> 00:26:44.019
I can't be in the hospital.

00:26:44.102 --> 00:26:47.189
-[David] Marcy.
-Listen to me.

00:26:47.272 --> 00:26:49.441
I have important work to do.

00:26:49.525 --> 00:26:50.692
At the library?

00:26:50.776 --> 00:26:54.321
No, not at the library.

00:26:54.404 --> 00:26:56.156
This is all happening
for a reason.

00:26:57.282 --> 00:26:58.534
Okay.

00:26:58.659 --> 00:27:02.246
How about I go get the doctor
and we can talk about this?

00:27:04.373 --> 00:27:05.791
Thank you.

00:27:05.916 --> 00:27:07.376
[David] Okay.

00:27:14.716 --> 00:27:17.344
[monitor pinging]

00:27:48.208 --> 00:27:49.459
[alert beeps]

00:27:56.425 --> 00:27:58.844
[beeping]

00:28:01.847 --> 00:28:02.973
[cell phone ringing]

00:28:03.098 --> 00:28:04.474
-Forbes.
-[MacLaren] <i>Hey.</i>

00:28:04.600 --> 00:28:06.018
How's Judge What's-His-Nuts?

00:28:06.101 --> 00:28:09.146
Still an asshole.
How's our potential shooter?

00:28:09.229 --> 00:28:11.356
Jonas Walker hasn't
left his house in a week.

00:28:11.440 --> 00:28:13.984
Starting to think we're wasting
our time on that one.

00:28:14.109 --> 00:28:15.986
Our chatroom,
on the other hand,

00:28:16.111 --> 00:28:18.989
has been filling up all day
with the same weird messages.

00:28:19.114 --> 00:28:20.782
I.P.s all over town.

00:28:20.866 --> 00:28:21.992
<i>You think it's something?</i>

00:28:22.117 --> 00:28:24.870
Gotta admit,
it's making me curious.

00:28:24.953 --> 00:28:26.413
The one who set up the chatroom

00:28:26.496 --> 00:28:28.457
was arrested
and released on a technicality.

00:28:28.540 --> 00:28:30.792
Might save time if you contact
the arresting officer.

00:28:30.876 --> 00:28:32.753
<i>Name's Gower.</i>

00:28:32.836 --> 00:28:35.130
Okay. Bright and early.

00:28:44.890 --> 00:28:46.892
[beeping]

00:28:57.653 --> 00:28:59.571
Marcy, what're you doing here?

00:28:59.655 --> 00:29:01.657
I was at your apartment!
I've been worried!

00:29:01.782 --> 00:29:04.284
I didn't know where else to go.

00:29:04.368 --> 00:29:06.286
What is going on?

00:29:07.287 --> 00:29:08.288
Tell me.

00:29:08.372 --> 00:29:10.415
I can't.

00:29:10.499 --> 00:29:11.541
A mistake's been made,

00:29:11.667 --> 00:29:13.919
and I'm not sure
how to correct it.

00:29:14.002 --> 00:29:16.421
I don't even know if it can be.

00:29:17.339 --> 00:29:20.050
Just... know
that I'm playing a small part

00:29:20.133 --> 00:29:21.426
in something that's important.

00:29:21.551 --> 00:29:23.178
Well, what does that even mean?

00:29:23.262 --> 00:29:25.305
[Marcy] I couldn't explain it
if I tried.

00:29:25.389 --> 00:29:29.393
Please...
just trust me anyway.

00:30:01.300 --> 00:30:03.593
[MacLaren] Morning.
Sorry to bother you so early.

00:30:03.719 --> 00:30:05.971
I'm Special Agent Grant MacLaren
with the FBI.

00:30:06.096 --> 00:30:08.098
FBI? Really?

00:30:08.181 --> 00:30:09.474
Really.

00:30:09.558 --> 00:30:11.852
A message was sent
from this I.P. address--

00:30:11.935 --> 00:30:14.271
that just means one of
the computers in your house--

00:30:14.354 --> 00:30:15.981
kinda raised
a flag in our system.

00:30:16.106 --> 00:30:18.358
Please tell me
this is not about Internet porn.

00:30:18.483 --> 00:30:21.361
No. Not porn. At least,
I-I don't think so.

00:30:21.445 --> 00:30:24.656
No, this is more
of a chatroom conversation.

00:30:24.740 --> 00:30:28.493
Ah. My son's always
in those rooms.

00:30:28.618 --> 00:30:30.871
Is he a gamer, by any chance?
Video games?

00:30:30.996 --> 00:30:32.539
[mom]
It's all he ever does.

00:30:32.622 --> 00:30:35.876
That, and the other thing.

00:30:35.959 --> 00:30:37.502
When do you expect him home?

00:30:37.586 --> 00:30:40.380
[mom] Said he'd be out
late tonight with friends.

00:30:40.464 --> 00:30:43.050
Is he in any kind of trouble?

00:30:43.133 --> 00:30:46.011
Nah. I doubt it.
You have a good day.

00:30:46.136 --> 00:30:49.348
[school bell rings]

00:30:58.106 --> 00:30:59.316
[girls giggling]

00:30:59.399 --> 00:31:01.443
[male student]
Hey. What're you doing here?

00:31:01.526 --> 00:31:02.527
What do you mean?

00:31:02.652 --> 00:31:03.779
You got a free ticket

00:31:03.862 --> 00:31:06.156
to stay home
for the rest of the year.

00:31:06.281 --> 00:31:07.949
And fail to graduate?

00:31:08.033 --> 00:31:09.534
Yeah,
like that was gonna happen!

00:31:09.659 --> 00:31:12.037
Can I ask you something
without telling everyone?

00:31:12.120 --> 00:31:13.205
-Yeah.
-Honestly?

00:31:13.288 --> 00:31:16.792
-Yeah, God, what is it?
-Which locker is mine?

00:31:16.875 --> 00:31:18.293
Holy shit.

00:31:18.377 --> 00:31:20.170
You mean you got,
like, brain damage?

00:31:20.253 --> 00:31:21.797
Post-concussion syndrome.

00:31:22.923 --> 00:31:24.299
Yeah.

00:31:24.424 --> 00:31:26.802
It's, uh...
it's right here.

00:31:31.306 --> 00:31:33.100
You want me
to show you the combo?

00:31:33.183 --> 00:31:34.518
Please.

00:31:41.191 --> 00:31:43.527
-[dishes clinking]
-[groans softly]

00:31:48.949 --> 00:31:49.950
[David] Hey.

00:31:50.033 --> 00:31:51.993
[Marcy] Why is this body
always so tired?

00:31:52.077 --> 00:31:53.995
"This body"?

00:31:54.079 --> 00:31:56.498
Well, maybe
'cause it works nights.

00:31:56.581 --> 00:31:58.834
This body just made breakfast.

00:31:58.959 --> 00:32:00.127
That's very kind.

00:32:00.210 --> 00:32:02.212
And you're naked again.

00:32:03.338 --> 00:32:05.340
Okay.

00:32:05.424 --> 00:32:07.467
How about you get dressed
before joining me?

00:32:10.220 --> 00:32:11.096
David?

00:32:13.598 --> 00:32:16.726
If I could tell you, I would.

00:32:18.103 --> 00:32:19.980
Hey, as long as
you're not an assassin

00:32:20.105 --> 00:32:24.025
or a Hollywood actress
researching a character.

00:32:24.109 --> 00:32:25.861
Those--
Those are the...

00:32:25.986 --> 00:32:27.904
two worst-case scenarios
I came up with

00:32:27.988 --> 00:32:29.739
while I was laying
awake all night.

00:32:39.833 --> 00:32:42.127
[cell phone ringing]

00:32:44.254 --> 00:32:46.006
[Detective Gower, over phone]
<i>Gower.</i>

00:32:46.131 --> 00:32:47.883
Morning.
Grant MacLaren, FBI.

00:32:47.966 --> 00:32:51.553
I'm investigating a 20-year-old
male you booked yesterday--

00:32:51.636 --> 00:32:53.555
-Philip Pearson, yeah.
-That's him.

00:32:53.638 --> 00:32:56.516
<i>Well, I guess you heard he won</i>
<i>the lottery yesterday, huh?</i>

00:32:56.600 --> 00:32:59.769
-You had to drop the charges?
-No, he won the fucking lottery.

00:32:59.853 --> 00:33:02.022
<i>Six numbers outta seven.</i>
<i>92-grand and change.</i>

00:33:02.105 --> 00:33:03.273
Lucky kid.

00:33:03.356 --> 00:33:06.818
Not if I catch him with that bag of smack
he's walking around with.

00:33:06.902 --> 00:33:10.071
Our system red-flagged him as
a potential member of a terrorist cell.

00:33:10.155 --> 00:33:12.032
I got the rest of the suspects
covered,

00:33:12.115 --> 00:33:13.909
<i>but if you could watch</i>
<i>this one--</i>

00:33:14.034 --> 00:33:16.912
Agent MacLaren, there's no way
in hell this kid's a terrorist.

00:33:16.995 --> 00:33:19.664
Yeah? What were the odds
he was gonna win the lottery?

00:33:20.290 --> 00:33:21.666
[sighs] Okay.

00:33:21.750 --> 00:33:23.793
Keep this number
and check in with me later.

00:33:23.919 --> 00:33:25.795
Tomorrow, he's all yours.

00:33:32.385 --> 00:33:34.554
Mm! You like that, sweetie?

00:33:34.638 --> 00:33:36.598
[knocking on door]

00:33:39.684 --> 00:33:41.186
Yes?

00:33:41.269 --> 00:33:44.189
Special Agent MacLaren
of the FBI.

00:33:44.272 --> 00:33:46.942
-Sorry to bother you.
-"MacLaren"?

00:33:47.067 --> 00:33:48.693
How can I help you?

00:33:48.777 --> 00:33:51.446
Our computer spits stuff out,
we have to follow it up.

00:33:51.530 --> 00:33:53.865
-Do you live here alone?
-With my son.

00:33:53.949 --> 00:33:56.326
-How old is he?
-Just over a year.

00:33:56.451 --> 00:33:59.454
So, no criminal record?

00:33:59.579 --> 00:34:00.455
Sorry.

00:34:00.539 --> 00:34:03.708
I probably
know the answer to this,

00:34:03.792 --> 00:34:07.212
but do you have plans
for later tonight downtown?

00:34:07.337 --> 00:34:09.965
No. No plans.

00:34:11.049 --> 00:34:12.801
You don't sound very sure.

00:34:14.553 --> 00:34:17.430
I was trying to decide
if you were asking me out.

00:34:17.514 --> 00:34:19.558
[chuckles] Uh, no.

00:34:19.641 --> 00:34:22.394
Me? I'm--
I'm busy tonight.

00:34:25.313 --> 00:34:26.273
Thanks for your time.

00:34:49.337 --> 00:34:50.880
[Gower] Hey! Pearson!

00:34:50.964 --> 00:34:54.134
I wonder how much smack
you can buy with 90 grand.

00:34:54.217 --> 00:34:56.094
The money's for something else.

00:34:56.219 --> 00:34:59.306
Save me the trouble of following
you and just tell me.

00:35:03.852 --> 00:35:06.229
I'm financing a secret hideout.

00:35:07.355 --> 00:35:10.483
Sorry, kid, you're gonna
have to do better than that.

00:35:18.992 --> 00:35:21.244
[David] You're welcome
to stay while I'm at work.

00:35:21.369 --> 00:35:24.372
-There's nothing in the fridge--
-I'll be out before you're home.

00:35:24.497 --> 00:35:27.000
I'd like to come back tonight,
if that's all right.

00:35:27.125 --> 00:35:29.002
It'll be late, though.

00:35:29.085 --> 00:35:31.004
I could come with you.

00:35:31.087 --> 00:35:35.133
No. No, you should
stay home tonight.

00:35:36.968 --> 00:35:38.511
The streets won't be safe.

00:35:40.263 --> 00:35:45.477
Wh-- What?
What's gonna happen?

00:35:47.395 --> 00:35:49.397
Oh, come on,
that's going too far.

00:35:49.481 --> 00:35:52.025
-I shouldn't have said anything.
-You can't expect me to--

00:35:58.657 --> 00:36:01.159
[Marcy] I'll be back
just after midnight.

00:36:02.744 --> 00:36:04.871
You're Batgirl, aren't you?

00:36:07.916 --> 00:36:09.542
Bye.

00:36:24.057 --> 00:36:25.183
[door shuts]

00:36:39.572 --> 00:36:42.200
[knocking on door]

00:37:11.438 --> 00:37:14.858
[♪♪♪]

00:37:38.006 --> 00:37:40.258
[keys clacking]

00:37:44.763 --> 00:37:46.473
[siren chirps]

00:37:59.402 --> 00:38:02.155
[thud]

00:38:02.280 --> 00:38:03.782
-[siren chirps]
-Shit!

00:38:03.907 --> 00:38:06.034
[engine starts, siren wails]

00:38:06.159 --> 00:38:07.410
[whistling]

00:38:08.536 --> 00:38:10.205
Come here.

00:38:10.288 --> 00:38:11.790
You're welcome.

00:38:11.873 --> 00:38:14.125
Get in. Let's go.
Come on.

00:38:15.919 --> 00:38:19.422
Had to pay a kid to dare a kid
to get Gower off your ass.

00:38:19.547 --> 00:38:21.341
Watching your back's
getting expensive, Philip.

00:38:21.424 --> 00:38:24.052
-What do you want in return?
-Today's bet.

00:38:24.177 --> 00:38:25.470
I can't do it.

00:38:25.553 --> 00:38:28.181
Yesterday, you gave me three.
I'm only asking for one.

00:38:28.306 --> 00:38:29.307
Yesterday was an emergency.

00:38:29.432 --> 00:38:31.726
Today's kind of
an emergency for me.

00:38:31.810 --> 00:38:35.063
Then you are a very bad gambler.

00:38:35.188 --> 00:38:37.732
Yeah, I'm a bad gambler...

00:38:37.816 --> 00:38:40.318
[tires squealing]

00:38:45.323 --> 00:38:46.449
[brakes screech]

00:38:46.533 --> 00:38:48.451
Maybe you'd like
to think about it.

00:38:48.535 --> 00:38:50.578
Get out.

00:38:56.668 --> 00:38:58.461
[Gower] Pearson! Come here!

00:39:00.672 --> 00:39:01.714
[cackles]

00:39:16.980 --> 00:39:18.982
-Where are you going?
-Out.

00:39:19.107 --> 00:39:20.733
With that guy?

00:39:28.825 --> 00:39:30.285
I don't have time for this.

00:39:30.368 --> 00:39:31.744
Well, make time.

00:39:31.828 --> 00:39:33.413
[gasps in pain]

00:39:33.496 --> 00:39:35.623
[gasping]

00:39:35.707 --> 00:39:36.749
Okay! Damn it.

00:39:36.875 --> 00:39:38.877
Last warning.

00:39:39.961 --> 00:39:40.837
Okay.

00:39:50.638 --> 00:39:52.974
[Jeff cries out]

00:40:01.149 --> 00:40:04.152
Hey! Hey!

00:40:08.615 --> 00:40:10.783
Pearson! Stop!

00:40:12.619 --> 00:40:14.621
Come on! Stop!

00:40:16.247 --> 00:40:18.082
[Gower wheezing]

00:40:18.166 --> 00:40:20.168
It's a good thing
you stopped, kiddo.

00:40:24.422 --> 00:40:28.092
If I had to climb that fence,
I was gonna have a heart attack.

00:40:28.176 --> 00:40:29.802
[Gower groans]

00:40:29.928 --> 00:40:31.679
You're having one right now.

00:40:31.804 --> 00:40:32.805
[Gower] Oh, shut up.

00:40:32.931 --> 00:40:36.559
I just need to catch my breath,
that's all.

00:40:38.686 --> 00:40:40.563
Ooh!

00:40:40.647 --> 00:40:42.857
Maybe you're right.

00:40:42.941 --> 00:40:45.318
My phone--
it's in the car.

00:40:45.401 --> 00:40:47.570
-Help me.
-I can't, Mr. Gower.

00:40:47.695 --> 00:40:50.490
[Gower] Then find someone
with a phone!

00:40:50.573 --> 00:40:51.741
I can't, I'm sorry.

00:40:51.824 --> 00:40:54.202
[Gower] You can. I won't
come after you, I promise.

00:40:54.285 --> 00:40:55.954
You're supposed to die
this afternoon.

00:40:56.037 --> 00:40:57.830
[Gower] No, you don't know--

00:40:57.914 --> 00:41:00.500
I knew the moment
that I heard your name.

00:41:00.583 --> 00:41:03.836
-I just didn't know I'd be here.
-Call 911 and go!

00:41:03.962 --> 00:41:07.966
Because we considered you
as a host.

00:41:08.049 --> 00:41:10.718
The heart attack
was inevitable within days.

00:41:10.802 --> 00:41:12.095
[Gower wheezing]

00:41:12.220 --> 00:41:15.223
No... I'm okay.

00:41:18.726 --> 00:41:20.812
I think I'm okay.

00:41:31.739 --> 00:41:32.740
[Philip sobs]

00:41:37.620 --> 00:41:39.330
[sobs]

00:41:46.254 --> 00:41:48.381
[phone ringing]

00:41:55.263 --> 00:41:56.806
Hello?

00:41:56.889 --> 00:41:59.642
-[MacLaren] <i>David Mailer?</i>
-Yeah?

00:41:59.726 --> 00:42:01.936
Special Agent
Grant MacLaren with the FBI.

00:42:02.020 --> 00:42:04.856
I came by earlier,
left a card under your door.

00:42:06.024 --> 00:42:07.900
Oh, sorry, I didn't, uh...

00:42:08.026 --> 00:42:10.653
-I didn't see it.
-Not a problem.

00:42:10.737 --> 00:42:12.321
Just following up
on a chatroom message

00:42:12.405 --> 00:42:14.782
that was sent from
your I.P. address last night.

00:42:14.866 --> 00:42:16.659
You mean my computer?

00:42:16.784 --> 00:42:19.412
<i>Right. Tell me, do you have</i>
<i>plans to meet anyone tonight</i>

00:42:19.537 --> 00:42:21.205
downtown,
on the 12th floor

00:42:21.289 --> 00:42:23.916
of an abandoned building,
about 11:17?

00:42:24.000 --> 00:42:26.169
No. Why--
Why would I do that?

00:42:26.252 --> 00:42:28.713
I guess that means
I won't be seeing you there.

00:42:28.796 --> 00:42:30.173
I'm just thinking out loud,

00:42:30.298 --> 00:42:32.925
but sometimes I let neighbors
use my Wi-Fi. Maybe that's, um--

00:42:33.051 --> 00:42:36.179
Well, that's a federal offense,
Mr. Mailer.

00:42:36.262 --> 00:42:38.556
[chuckles]

00:42:38.639 --> 00:42:39.557
Is it?

00:42:39.682 --> 00:42:41.893
No. I'm kidding.
Have a good evening.

00:43:27.688 --> 00:43:29.232
No. I'm not pressing charges.

00:43:29.315 --> 00:43:31.651
I just want to know
where she took it.

00:43:31.734 --> 00:43:34.195
Well, just check
and keep your mouth shut.

00:43:38.616 --> 00:43:40.618
All right. Thanks.

00:43:47.959 --> 00:43:50.503
[distant sirens]

00:43:55.633 --> 00:43:57.093
[dials cell phone]

00:43:59.011 --> 00:44:00.388
Hello?

00:44:00.513 --> 00:44:03.432
I'm-- I'm trying to reach
Detective Gower.

00:44:03.516 --> 00:44:05.643
I thought this was his--

00:44:06.727 --> 00:44:08.563
Jesus, I'm sorry to hear that.

00:44:08.646 --> 00:44:12.275
No, it's-it's not important.
Um, thank you.

00:44:39.051 --> 00:44:40.761
Carly?

00:44:45.433 --> 00:44:46.642
[remote lock beeps]

00:45:13.586 --> 00:45:15.212
Carly?

00:45:42.740 --> 00:45:45.368
[distant sirens]

00:46:09.350 --> 00:46:10.893
[ticking]

00:46:22.780 --> 00:46:24.407
[cell phone rings]

00:46:25.408 --> 00:46:27.034
[ringing]

00:46:35.418 --> 00:46:36.794
Got you.

00:46:36.919 --> 00:46:38.004
[exhales]

00:46:51.308 --> 00:46:52.935
You're actually all here.

00:46:53.894 --> 00:46:55.354
[Carly]
We've been waiting for you.

00:46:55.438 --> 00:46:56.689
[MacLaren] Uh-huh.

00:46:56.772 --> 00:46:58.065
Where's the social worker?

00:46:58.190 --> 00:47:00.818
-David isn't one of us.
-One of--?

00:47:00.901 --> 00:47:02.820
We're travelers from the future,
Agent MacLaren.

00:47:02.903 --> 00:47:04.822
[Marcy] In our time,
many years from now,

00:47:04.947 --> 00:47:07.700
humanity's been
all but wiped out.

00:47:07.825 --> 00:47:09.326
We've come back to change that.

00:47:09.410 --> 00:47:12.747
There are thousands of travelers
already here taking part.

00:47:13.372 --> 00:47:14.665
Huh.

00:47:15.958 --> 00:47:19.378
Okay, what do you say
we, uh, travel downstairs

00:47:19.462 --> 00:47:20.963
and talk about this
somewhere else?

00:47:21.088 --> 00:47:22.089
It's not safe here.

00:47:27.219 --> 00:47:28.345
60 seconds.

00:47:28.429 --> 00:47:29.722
Till what?

00:47:29.805 --> 00:47:31.932
[Philip] In the future,
we've developed a technology

00:47:32.016 --> 00:47:35.728
that allows a traveler to project his
or her conscious mind into a host body

00:47:35.811 --> 00:47:40.149
by knowing the precise time, elevation,
latitude, and longitude of their death.

00:47:40.232 --> 00:47:41.150
[MacLaren] "T.E.L.L."

00:47:41.233 --> 00:47:42.485
[Marcy]
A Traveler's consciousness

00:47:42.610 --> 00:47:45.154
arrives moments before
that historical time of death,

00:47:45.237 --> 00:47:47.615
overriding
the original host's mind,

00:47:47.698 --> 00:47:50.493
then resumes his or her life
by using their knowledge

00:47:50.576 --> 00:47:52.244
of historical records
and social media.

00:47:52.328 --> 00:47:53.662
Okay, that's enough bullshit
for now--

00:47:53.746 --> 00:47:55.748
-30 seconds.
-Wait.

00:47:55.873 --> 00:47:57.833
Who the hell is that?

00:47:59.210 --> 00:48:02.004
That's the body of Jonas Walker.

00:48:03.255 --> 00:48:05.299
We stopped him from going
on a shooting rampage,

00:48:05.382 --> 00:48:09.386
as you tried and failed to do,
between 11:14 and 11:17.

00:48:09.512 --> 00:48:10.638
[Trevor] 20 seconds.

00:48:10.721 --> 00:48:12.807
[Carly]
We know the events of tonight

00:48:12.890 --> 00:48:14.266
because for us,
they've already happened.

00:48:14.391 --> 00:48:16.018
Just as we know
during a blackout,

00:48:16.102 --> 00:48:18.312
at 11:17,
in pursuit of Jonas Walker,

00:48:18.395 --> 00:48:19.772
Special Agent Grant MacLaren

00:48:19.897 --> 00:48:22.066
fell 45 meters
down an open elevator shaft

00:48:22.149 --> 00:48:24.151
to his death.

00:48:24.276 --> 00:48:25.653
Three seconds.

00:48:28.405 --> 00:48:29.907
[cell phone ringing]

00:48:32.034 --> 00:48:34.120
[ringing in MacLaren's head]

00:48:37.123 --> 00:48:40.751
[crying out in pain]

00:48:43.295 --> 00:48:46.090
Aah!

00:48:46.173 --> 00:48:49.552
[ringing and shrieking stop]

00:48:58.686 --> 00:49:00.396
I see we all made it.

00:49:03.816 --> 00:49:06.694
Let's begin.